"## Summary\n\nAgent-core follow-up 52: review r31's M-1, and members 23's request 2 for observation submission records.\n- **Session:** launched 09:08 EST on 2026-11-04 on `main` at `52b93845`, and delivered at 11:12.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 8 commits and 10 owned files, +1,717/−47.\n  - **The production change is in `node/agent`:**\n    - `observe.go`: the dedup exception and the new submission path;\n    - `recovery_renewal.go`: the shared binding predicate;\n    - `observation_log.go`: the two records, which is a new file;\n    - `engine.go`: one diagnostic map.\n  - **The rest:**\n    - r31's two proofs, imported;\n    - the lane's own proofs;\n    - the operator documentation in `docs/node/README.md`;\n    - the dated note `docs/node/followup52-2026-11-04.md`.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` after devstack 36 (#476, `034c82cf`) with this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/node.mk node-lint node-test node-test-integration node-build`;\n    - r31's four proofs by name, `TestR31_` over `node/agent` and `node/updater`;\n    - the R16 to r31 proofs over `node/agent`, `node/watchdog` and `node/enforce`;\n    - the lane's seven new tests by name, `TestF52_` and `TestD157_F52_`;\n    - `go test ./node/updater/... ./node/nodelock/...`;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...` and the committed-evidence tests;\n    - `go vet ./...`, `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** one ordinary lab in the lane's own prefix, with no rerun and no reservation. It waited 240 s for other lanes' runs first. Zero owned Docker objects at the end.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **The diagnosis came first (D-141),** committed on the unchanged base before any code (`edbd2a4b`). r31's three cases:\n  - **A, an isolation error in the report, is reachable and persistent.** A historical isolation containment stays across run Steps, and it caused the unchanged-report flood. A pending-revoke isolation is transient.\n  - **B, a failed meter path, is not reached through normal Steps.** Enforcement withdraws and disarms the recovery before the next observation. r31 constructed it directly.\n  - **C, a stale lease, is reachable for one enforcement pass,** including once after a rejected adoption. Retention refuses it at the next Step if the lease is still stale.\n  - Zero bindings alone do not start a closed recovery.\n- **The fix** (`dfcf28c1`) is one predicate, `canBindRecoveryReport`. It is extracted exactly from the existing binding rules, and both the binding and the dedup exception now use it.\n  - **At an unchanged state with a report pending,** the agent builds a new report only when an armed, unbound recovery can bind it. Otherwise ordinary dedup holds, and it reads neither the report nor the update journal.\n  - **Unchanged:**\n    - the report body;\n    - the 32-entry outbox;\n    - the cadence, retry, backoff and Retry-After;\n    - agent-core 51's unchanged-state binding, which its proof still covers;\n    - D-067, D-135/D-136, D-155/D-156 and D-157.\n- **r31's proofs** were imported byte-identically first (`376c9633`).\n  - **The updater file is still identical,** SHA-256 `00414c8f…`.\n  - **The agent file differs in two ways only.** Three comment labels change from `TODO` to `Regression`. And case C's setup now crosses the existing 30 s stale-lease alarm, a real state transition that the original baseline counted as a duplicate, and asserts it before taking its baseline.\n  - **Every imported assertion is kept,** and the dated note records the change. All three M-1 subtests fail on the unfixed code, and the held r31 proofs pass before and after.\n- **The lane's own proofs run whole Steps:**\n  - the persistent case runs 210 Steps at a 5 s run cadence, so 35 default 30 s observation intervals, and ends with one unchanged pending report and no `outbox_full`;\n  - the stale and pending-revoke cases run 35 TEST ONLY 1 s intervals after their transient recovery ends.\n- **The two records** (`36b1d814`), in the agent's existing log format, named in `docs/node/README.md`:\n  - **`observation enqueued`,** once per queued report: `report_id`, `observed_at` and `due_reason`. The reason is one of `closed_recovery_binding`, `first_report`, `serving_changed`, `state_changed` or `interval_elapsed`, in that precedence;\n  - **`observation submission`,** once per submission call:\n    - the report IDs, attempt numbers and attempt scope;\n    - `process_id` and `boot_id`;\n    - the start and duration;\n    - the outcome: `accepted`, `rejected`, `transport_error`, `timeout` or `unconfirmed_response`;\n    - the accepted IDs, HTTP status, Central's error code and a finite transport-error class;\n    - the next retry and `retry_after_ms`.\n  - **Attempt numbers count per report per process,** and `attempt_scope=process` says so. The outbox's durable counter is left as it is: it marks uncertainty, and a retryable failure increments it twice.\n  - **Never logged:** a report body, URL, error text, credential, token or key. A deduplicated enqueue, an idle Step or a waiting retry slot writes neither record.\n  - **Offline tests** use the fake control: accepted, a 5xx, a 429 with `Retry-After`, a transport error and a timeout.\n- **The lab: 13 of 13 pass,** under `fvpn-w2-agent-core-f52`.\n  - In `TestLabD087_D104_GrantRenewalExpiryCorrelation`'s expiry phase, the last positive left at D − 100.548 ms. The first drop reached ingress at D − 63.547 ms.\n  - Both new records appear in the lab's agent log. The dated note quotes one pair, with only the host boot ID redacted.\n- **No live claim.** Members' next assembled run reads the records on `main`, and devstack can read the same format.\n"
